; gfx942 has no packed f64 ALU, so a scalar fmul that feeds a fusable fadd is
; free. The vector fmul must not get that discount from the context of lane 0
; alone. In mixed_lanes the fmuls in lanes 1-3 have a second use and do not
; fuse, so the vector fmul is not free and the reduction must stay scalar.

define double @mixed_lanes(ptr noalias %e, ptr %a, ptr %b) {
